---
import { CANON_VERSION } from "../../canon.ts";
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
---
<Docs title="CLI — Specline">
  <div class="doc-kicker">Specline · CLI</div>
  <h1>CLI reference</h1>
  <p class="doc-lead">One umbrella command, <code>specline</code>, with six subcommands. <code>check</code> is the checker (and the default) — point it at a repo. <code>rules</code> and <code>spec</code> describe themselves and need no repo at all. Specline runs in <strong>one mode</strong>: it reports every finding and exits nonzero when any of them is an error.</p>

  <div class="codeblock">
    <div class="cb-bar"><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="fn">usage</span></div>
    <pre>specline check  [PATH] [--format json|human]
                       [--changed &lt;file&gt;...] [--modified &lt;file&gt;...] [--now &lt;iso-date&gt;]
specline rules  [PATH] [--format json|markdown]
specline spec   [PATH]
specline init   [PATH] [--decider &lt;name&gt;]
                       [--github-action | --no-github-action] [--check] [--yes]
specline sync   [PATH] [--check]
specline upgrade [PATH] [--check]</pre>
  </div>

  <h2>specline check</h2>
  <p>This is where the checking happens. Specline walks <code>docs/</code> beneath <code>PATH</code> (default <code>.</code>), runs Parts 1 and 2's rules (plus Part 3's, experimental, if <code>specline.yml</code> sets <code>unattended: true</code>), and emits findings. JSON is the source of truth; the human output is just a view onto it.</p>
  <div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table class="book-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>--format</td><td><code>human</code> (default at a terminal) or <code>json</code> (agents, CI).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>--changed</td><td>Repo-relative paths you touched. Spec-scoped integrity findings error only for specs in this set; otherwise they warn (quarantine).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>--modified</td><td>Repo-relative modified or removed paths for archive immutability. New archive files are graduation and should not be included.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>--now</td><td>Reference ISO date for time-dependent checks. Specline never reads the wall clock — determinism.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Exit codes</h3>
  <div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table class="book-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Means</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>0</td><td>No error-severity findings (warnings allowed); or a clean <code>--check</code> on <code>init</code>/<code>sync</code>/<code>upgrade</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>1</td><td>At least one error, or a stale <code>--check</code>. CI gates on this; agents parse the findings. The two never disagree.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2</td><td>Usage error (bad flag, no <code>docs/</code> found).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>3</td><td>Internal error — to stderr, never as malformed stdout.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Output contract</h3>
  <div class="codeblock">
    <div class="cb-bar"><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="fn">specline check . --format json</span></div>
    <pre><span class="dl">&#123;</span>
  <span class="k">"tool_version"</span>: <span class="v">"0.1.0"</span>,
  <span class="k">"canon"</span>: <span class="v">"{CANON_VERSION}"</span>,
  <span class="k">"unattended"</span>: <span class="v">false</span>,
  <span class="k">"summary"</span>: <span class="dl">&#123;</span> <span class="k">"errors"</span>: <span class="v">0</span>, <span class="k">"warnings"</span>: <span class="v">1</span>, <span class="k">"info"</span>: <span class="v">0</span> <span class="dl">&#125;</span>,
  <span class="k">"findings"</span>: <span class="dl">[</span> <span class="cmt">/* rule_id, severity, scope, file, line, message, fix_hint */</span> <span class="dl">]</span>
<span class="dl">&#125;</span></pre>
  </div>
  <p>The output never surprises you. Findings sort by <code>file</code>, then <code>line</code> (null first), then <code>rule_id</code> — so two runs on the same input and the same <code>--now</code> come out byte-identical.</p>

  <h2>specline rules</h2>
  <p>Prints the full <a href="/docs/rules">rule catalog</a> — every <code>rule_id</code> with its severity and scope — as <code>--format markdown</code> (default) or <code>json</code>. Reads <code>PATH</code>'s <code>specline.yml</code> for the <code>unattended</code> switch (default <code>.</code>); with it off, Part 3's rules are neither listed nor served.</p>

  <h2>specline spec</h2>
  <p>Prints the pinned canon to stdout, sliced at Part 3 unless <code>PATH</code>'s <code>specline.yml</code> sets <code>unattended: true</code>. Use it to drop Specline straight into an agent's context. (The web twin is <a href="/spec.md">/spec.md</a>.)</p>
  <h2>specline init / sync / upgrade</h2>
  <p><code>init</code> creates the starting documentation directories (<code>drafts/</code>, <code>specs/</code>, <code>knowledge/</code>, <code>archive/</code>, <code>conventions/</code>, <code>decisions/</code>, <code>strategy/</code>, <code>technical/</code>), authored starters, <code>specline.yml</code>, and an optional GitHub Action. Use <code>--yes</code> for noninteractive defaults. <code>sync</code> refreshes recognized generated artifacts in existing directories. <code>upgrade</code> updates the canon pin and refreshes generated artifacts — and maps a legacy <code>tier: 2</code> to <code>unattended: true</code>, dropping <code>tier: 0|1</code>. Existing authored content is preserved.</p>
  <p>All three accept <code>--check</code>: preview without writes, returning 1 when changes are needed and 0 when current. <code>doctor</code> remains a compatibility alias for <code>check</code>.</p>
</Docs>
